@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "provisioning.integration"

Feature:  Dossiera To Koroneiki Integration
	Testing to assure dossiera to koroneiki integration works properly.

Setup:
	* I get all test passwords and admin emails
	* I generate several static variables for Provisioning
	* I generate a provisioning company name
	* I generate a provisioning project name
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | pro.koroneiki1                       |
	| Email Address | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PRO                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki1                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | pro.koroneiki2                       |
	| Email Address | pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PRO                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki2                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | pro.koroneiki3                       |
	| Email Address | pro.koroneiki3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PRO                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki3                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | pro.koroneiki4                       |
	| Email Address | pro.koroneiki4@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PRO                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki4                           |

Teardown:
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the first default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Onepro - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the second default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Prokor - ${staticCompanyName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the third default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Proone - ${staticCompanyName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the fourth default user ID variable
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Korpro - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Onepro - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Prokor - ${staticCompanyName} |
	| Proone - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| PROKORKORPRO |
	| PROONEONEPRO |
	| PROKORONEPRO |
	| PROKOR       |
	| PROONE       |
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes via groovy
	| PROKORKORPRO |
	| PROONEONEPRO |
	| PROKORONEPRO |
	| PROKOR       |
	| PROONE       |
	* I tear down the products on koroneiki with the following names
	| A Liferay DXP Product    |
	| A Liferay Portal Product |
	| Random Subscription      |
	| Nonexistent Subscription |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from okta
	| pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pro.koroneiki3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pro.koroneiki4@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pro.koroneiki3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pro.koroneiki4@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from koroneiki
	| pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pro.koroneiki3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pro.koroneiki4@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pro.koroneiki3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pro.koroneiki4@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I teardown the tickets with the following keywords from zendesk.liferay.com
	| New Subscription(s) for Korpro - ${staticProjectName} |
	| New Subscription(s) for Onepro - ${staticProjectName} |
	| New Subscription(s) for Prokor - ${staticCompanyName} |
	| New Subscription(s) for Proone - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pro.koroneiki3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pro.koroneiki4@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com if still present
	| Korpro - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Onepro - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Prokor - ${staticCompanyName} |
	| Proone - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId1}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId2}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId3}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId4}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: Create entities
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	@ help.center.smoke = "true"
	Testing the ability to create a project in Dossiera and verifying that the respective entities get sent to and created in Koroneiki

	Given I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Prokor - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Contact First Name                     | PRO                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Owner First Name                       | PRO                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Koroneiki2                                 |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | Liferay Digital Enterprise - Prod Sizing 4 |
	| Project Name                           | Korpro - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki account with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" and the following values
	| Account Field and Value    | liferayVersion                       | DXP 7.1 | |
	| Code                       | PROKORKORPRO                         |         | |
	| Parent Account Name        | Prokor - ${staticCompanyName}        |         | |
	| Contact Email Address      | pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |         | |
	| Name                       | Korpro - ${staticProjectName}        |         | |
	| Region                     | United States                        |         | |
	| Language                   | English                              |         | |
	| Status                     | Active                               |         | |
	And I should be able to view a postal address on koroneiki for the account "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" with the street address "456 Fake Street" with the following values
	| Country               | United States   |
	| Locality              | Diamond Bar     |
	| Region                | California      |
	| Postal Code           | 91765           |
	| Street Address Line 1 | 456 Fake Street |
	And the external link with the entity id "${staticDossieraAccountKey}" and domain "salesforce" should be present on the account "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" with the following values
	| Domain      | salesforce                  |
	| Entity Id   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey} |
	| Entity Name | account                     |
	And the external link with the entity id "${staticDossieraProjectKey}" and domain "dossiera" should be present on the account "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" with the following values
	| Domain      | dossiera                    |
	| Entity Id   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey} |
	| Entity Name | project                     |
	And the external link with the entity id "${staticSalesforceProjectKey}" should be present on the account "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" with the following values
	| Domain      | salesforce                    |
	| Entity Id   | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey} |
	| Entity Name | project                       |
	And the external link with the entity id "${staticDossieraAccountKey}" and domain "salesforce" should be present on the account "Prokor - ${staticCompanyName}" with the following values
	| Domain      | salesforce                  |
	| Entity Id   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey} |
	| Entity Name | account                     |
	And the external link with the entity id "${staticDossieraAccountKey}" and domain "dossiera" should be present on the account "Prokor - ${staticCompanyName}" with the following values
	| Domain      | dossiera                    |
	| Entity Id   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey} |
	| Entity Name | account                     |
	And the external link with the entity id "${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}" should be present on the product purchase made by account "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "DXP Production" with the following values
	| Domain      | salesforce                        |
	| Entity Id   | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey} |
	| Entity Name | opportunity                       |
	And the external link with the entity id "${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}" should be present on the product purchase made by account "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "Platinum Subscription" with the following values
	| Domain      | salesforce                        |
	| Entity Id   | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey} |
	| Entity Name | opportunity                       |
	And I should be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the following values
	| Email Address | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PRO                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki1                           |
	And I should be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the following values
	| Email Address | pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PRO                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki2                           |
	And the contact with the email address "pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the account "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" should have the contact role "Support User"
	And the contact with the email address "pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the account "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" should have the contact role "Liferay Sales"
	And the contact with the email address "pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the account "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" should have the contact role "Secondary Contact"
	And I should be able to view a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "DXP Production" with the following values
	| Quantity | 1        | |
	| Status   | Approved | |
	And I should be able to view a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "Platinum Subscription" with the following values
	| Quantity | 1        | |
	| Status   | Approved | |

Scenario: Send subsequent message after initial project with blank support region
	Testing the ability to create a project with no support region in Dossiera before sending a subsequent message with the support region and verifying that the respective entities get sent to and created in Koroneiki

	Given I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code   | PROKOR                        | |
	| Name   | Prokor - ${staticCompanyName} | |
	| Status | Active                        | |
	And I create a child account for an account with the name "Prokor - ${staticCompanyName}" on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code   | PROKORKORPRO                  | |
	| Name   | Korpro - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Status | Active                        | |
	| Tier   | T4                            | |
	And I create an external link for the account "Prokor - ${staticCompanyName}" with the following values
	| Domain      | salesforce                  |
	| Entity Id   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey} |
	| Entity Name | account                     |
	And I create an external link for the account "Prokor - ${staticCompanyName}" with the following values
	| Domain      | dossiera                    |
	| Entity Id   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey} |
	| Entity Name | account                     |
	And I create an external link for the account "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" with the following values
	| Domain      | salesforce                  |
	| Entity Id   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey} |
	| Entity Name | account                     |
	And I create an external link for the account "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" with the following values
	| Domain      | dossiera                    |
	| Entity Id   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey} |
	| Entity Name | project                     |
	And I create an external link for the account "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" with the following values
	| Domain      | salesforce                    |
	| Entity Id   | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey} |
	| Entity Name | project                       |
	And I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Prokor - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Contact First Name                     | PRO                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Owner First Name                       | PRO                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Koroneiki2                                 |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | Liferay Digital Enterprise - Prod Sizing 4 |
	| Project Name                           | Korpro - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki account with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" and the following values
	| Code                       | PROKORKORPRO                         | | |
	| Parent Account Name        | Prokor - ${staticCompanyName}        | | |
	| Contact Email Address      | pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken | | |
	| Name                       | Korpro - ${staticProjectName}        | | |
	| Region                     | United States                        | | |
	| Status                     | Active                               | | |
	And the external link with the entity id "${staticDossieraAccountKey}" and domain "salesforce" should be present on the account "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" with the following values
	| Domain      | salesforce                  |
	| Entity Id   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey} |
	| Entity Name | account                     |
	And the external link with the entity id "${staticDossieraProjectKey}" and domain "dossiera" should be present on the account "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" with the following values
	| Domain      | dossiera                    |
	| Entity Id   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey} |
	| Entity Name | project                     |
	And the external link with the entity id "${staticSalesforceProjectKey}" should be present on the account "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" with the following values
	| Domain      | salesforce                    |
	| Entity Id   | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey} |
	| Entity Name | project                       |
	And the external link with the entity id "${staticDossieraAccountKey}" and domain "salesforce" should be present on the account "Prokor - ${staticCompanyName}" with the following values
	| Domain      | salesforce                  |
	| Entity Id   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey} |
	| Entity Name | account                     |
	And the external link with the entity id "${staticDossieraAccountKey}" and domain "dossiera" should be present on the account "Prokor - ${staticCompanyName}" with the following values
	| Domain      | dossiera                    |
	| Entity Id   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey} |
	| Entity Name | account                     |
	And the external link with the entity id "${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}" should be present on the product purchase made by account "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "DXP Production" with the following values
	| Domain      | salesforce                        |
	| Entity Id   | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey} |
	| Entity Name | opportunity                       |
	And the external link with the entity id "${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}" should be present on the product purchase made by account "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "Platinum Subscription" with the following values
	| Domain      | salesforce                        |
	| Entity Id   | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey} |
	| Entity Name | opportunity                       |
	And I should be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the following values
	| Email Address | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PRO                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki1                           |
	And I should be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the following values
	| Email Address | pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PRO                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki2                           |
	And the contact with the email address "pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the account "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" should have the contact role "Support User"
	And the contact with the email address "pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the account "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" should have the contact role "Liferay Sales"
	And the contact with the email address "pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the account "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" should have the contact role "Secondary Contact"
	And I should be able to view a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "DXP Production" with the following values
	| Quantity | 1        | |
	| Status   | Approved | |
	And I should be able to view a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "Platinum Subscription" with the following values
	| Quantity | 1        | |
	| Status   | Approved | |
	When I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticKoroneikiAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticKoroneikiAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korpro"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the Sync To Zendesk button on the account page
	Then the support organization with the code "PROKORKORPRO" should be part of the support site
	When I wait for "3" minutes
	Then the organization "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the account with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" should have "4" external links
	And the account with the name "Prokor - ${staticCompanyName}" should have "2" external links

Scenario: Send message with existing product and contact entities
	Testing the ability to create a project in Dossiera and verifying that the existing product and contact entities on Koroneiki get used

	Given I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PRO                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki1                           |
	And I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PRO                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki2                           |
	And I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay DXP Product | |
	And I create an external link on a product "A Liferay DXP Product" with the following values
	| Domain      | dossiera              |
	| Entity Id   | A Liferay DXP Product |
	| Entity Name | product               |
	And I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Prokor - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Contact First Name                     | PRO                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Owner First Name                       | PRO                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Koroneiki2                                 |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | A Liferay DXP Product                      |
	| Project Name                           | Korpro - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki account with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" and the following values
	| Account Field and Value    | liferayVersion                       | DXP 7.1 | |
	| Code                       | PROKORKORPRO                         |         | |
	| Parent Account Name        | Prokor - ${staticCompanyName}        |         | |
	| Contact Email Address      | pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |         | |
	| Name                       | Korpro - ${staticProjectName}        |         | |
	| Region                     | United States                        |         | |
	| Status                     | Active                               |         | |
	And I should be able to view a postal address on koroneiki for the account "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" with the street address "456 Fake Street" with the following values
	| Country               | United States   |
	| Locality              | Diamond Bar     |
	| Region                | California      |
	| Postal Code           | 91765           |
	| Street Address Line 1 | 456 Fake Street |
	And the external link with the entity id "${staticDossieraAccountKey}" and domain "salesforce" should be present on the account "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" with the following values
	| Domain      | salesforce                  |
	| Entity Id   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey} |
	| Entity Name | account                     |
	And the external link with the entity id "${staticDossieraProjectKey}" and domain "dossiera" should be present on the account "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" with the following values
	| Domain      | dossiera                    |
	| Entity Id   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey} |
	| Entity Name | project                     |
	And the external link with the entity id "${staticSalesforceProjectKey}" should be present on the account "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" with the following values
	| Domain      | salesforce                    |
	| Entity Id   | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey} |
	| Entity Name | project                       |
